        <mxCell id="4388jJ7OOFdwEJkS5ykN-14" value="1. Adam mentioned some of the sites are &#39;fishy&#39;&lt;br&gt;2. Also he mentioned some of the sites are higher maintenance then other because they periodically change stuff like class names&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. We need to strive for a balanced or slightly unbalanced dataset, meaning&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;we need to check each site and determine which algorithm it uses&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;and then choose which sites to use&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Eventually we probably won&#39;t use the whole 1000 websites, but we need to strive&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;to use as much as possible&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-790" y="570" width="440" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="4388jJ7OOFdwEJkS5ykN-15" value="What each container requires?&lt;br&gt;Sender:&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Getting the relevant domain from the switcher&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Creating a versatile platform how to interact correctly with the given domain&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;Switcher:&lt;br&gt;1. Manage which domain ran already&lt;br&gt;and run the next one correctly&lt;br&gt;2. Ask Amit+Bar - do we always run through all the domain? If not then how&lt;br&gt;do we manage that in the framework?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Domain maintainer:&lt;br&gt;New container!&lt;br&gt;The containers responsibility is handling Get requests from the other containers&lt;br&gt;and making sure the websites datasheet&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;is still relevant, and try to fix it if it isn&#39;t&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
